summary:
  A variable named `final` — a reserved word on Qt 6.10.

history:
  2026-08-03, released as 2026.24: `var final` parsed fine on the rolling Qt we
  develop against and killed the widget outright on Kubuntu 26.04 LTS, which
  ships Qt 6.10. Fixed in 2026.25 and locked down by an invariant plus the
  lts-parse CI job — this mutant is what proves both still work.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
    function _pad2(n) {

replace:
    function _pad2(final) {

expect:
  tests/test_invariants.py::test_no_reserved_word_is_used_as_an_identifier, and
  the LTS Qt parse job in CI.
